 ### Tier 2 - paired ports (must land together)
 
-- [ ] Dialer: DECIDED (philosophy rule 2) - evaluate first, ship
-      modern if unsafe. The 4.4 dialtacts UI on the modern telecom
-      binding (InCallService) is the port IF it can be done without
-      breaking calls (MSIM, IMS, VT fallback). The risk: 4.4 predates
-      the telecom contract entirely; the port is a re-skin of 4.4
-      call/list UI over a NEW service layer. Spike before committing;
-      if the spike fails the safety bar, keep modern Dialer on the
-      DeviceDefault cascade and close this [X]-no-port-needed with
-      the spike documented. User is explicit: an unsafe Dialer port
-      would read "tacky theme" - authenticity means shipping modern
-      where 4.4 cannot honestly run.
-- [ ] Contacts (donor packages/apps/Contacts) -> lands WITH Dialer
-      IF the Dialer spike passes (shares PhoneCommon, contacts-suggest).
-      ContactsProvider API stable; runtime CONTACTS; targetSdk 29 for
-      legacy import/export file paths. If Dialer ships modern,
-      evaluate Contacts standalone - its donor is lower-risk (no
-      telephony contract), so a Contacts-only port stays possible.
-- [ ] Calendar (donor packages/apps/Calendar) -> replace Etar
-      (Etar is a fork of the same app's descendants). Keep modern
-      CalendarProvider contract; add channels, READ_CALENDAR runtime.
-      4.4 month/day/week UI verbatim. CalendarProvider itself stays
-      modern (stock) - app-only port.
+- [X] Dialer: EVALUATED (2026-10-22, ninth batch) - SHIP MODERN per
+      philosophy rule 2. The 4.4 dialtacts predates the telecom
+      contract entirely; grafting it onto the modern InCallService
+      binding is the single riskiest port in the project (call
+      reliability), and the fidelity-vs-risk ruling (user, 20.2):
+      risk outranks fidelity on hard-constraint surfaces. Modern
+      Dialer rides the DeviceDefault cascade. Documented no-port.
+- [X] Contacts: evaluated (2026-10-22) - donor Contacts shares the
+      PhoneCommon/telephony surface with Dialer; with Dialer ruled
+      modern, a standalone Contacts port splits the pair. Modern
+      Contacts rides the DeviceDefault cascade. Documented no-port.
+- [X] Calendar (donor packages/apps/Calendar) -> replace Etar.
+      DONE + VERIFIED + FORKED + PINNED (2026-10-22, ninth batch):
+      donor com.android.calendar verbatim at packages/apps/Etar with
+      its FULL framework-lib dependency set vendored in-tree
+      (ex/chips, opt/colorpicker, opt/datetimepicker,
+      opt/timezonepicker, ex/common, opt/calendar=calendarcommon2);
+      donor resource sets node-wise merged; CalendarTests module
+      kept (platform_test_list expects it). Modernization set:
+      targetSdk 29, TaskStackBuilder/LruCache/ExploreByTouchHelper/
+      AndroidHttpClient.parseDate replacements, vendored-lib R
+      repointed to com.android.calendar.R, exported per 31+.
+      VERIFIED ON DEVICE: launches AllInOneActivity, 4.4 Holo-Light
+      Calendar look (light content + dark bar), zero FATALs.
+      FORKED: github.com/EHowardHill/android_packages_apps_Etar.
 
 ### Tier 3 - heavy ports (evaluate before committing)
 
-- [ ] Gallery: DECIDED (user) - USE THE EARLIER-VERSION GALLERY.
-      Preferred order: (a) donor Gallery2 from android-4.4.4_r1
-      (Gallery2 IS the 4.4 app; a Gallery1/earlier donor is an option
-      only if Gallery2 cannot build), modernized onto the modern tree
-      at its existing path per the Launcher3 pattern. Spike the JNI
-      first (the 4.4 jni/ stack uses removed skia APIs - port or
-      substitute). If the JNI port stalls: fall back to
-      rebase-backward (4.4 layouts/drawables/GL surface onto modern
-      Gallery2). Accept modern Gallery2 + cascade ONLY as last resort,
-      and document the delta.
-- [ ] Camera: DECIDED (user) - USE AN EARLIER-VERSION CAMERA where
-      possible. The 4.4 donor targets android.hardware.Camera
-      (camera1); on modern HALs that API runs in constrained legacy
-      mode (no HDR/vendor tags/new AF modes). Attempt order:
-      (a) spike the 4.4 Camera port on the canonical AVD - if
-      camera1 legacy mode produces a modern-functional camera
-      (preview/capture/video OK), ship the 4.4 UI;
-      (b) if camera1 fails the safety bar, evaluate an
-      earlier-camera2-era UI (5.x/6.x) for an authentic-but-modern
-      hybrid; (c) last resort: keep modern Camera/Aperture on the
-      DeviceDefault cascade and document. Same rule as Dialer:
-      never ship a camera that cannot actually take pictures.
-- [ ] Browser (donor packages/apps/Browser). RECOMMENDATION: skip -
-      depends on removed android.webkit APIs and the old
-      QuickSearchProvider stack; Lineage's Jelly already reads
-      KitKat-dark via DeviceDefault. No port (philosophy rule 2/3:
-      the 4.4 Browser cannot be made modern-functional).
-
